SURFACE SUMMARY (web → native, 1:1)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
StatusPageSkeleton is the layout-shaped loading state the System Status page renders during its initial fetch. It is
a PURE presentational component: the web source owns no data, fires no hook, makes no t() call, and has NO
conditional render branch — it IS the page's `loading` state (the empty / error / stale / offline states belong to
the parent page that swaps this skeleton out once its query resolves). Reproduced child-for-child from the web root
`space-y-5 max-w-3xl mx-auto` (nine stacked children), mapped to platform tokens (no Tailwind ported):

  region[0] hero          GlassPanel.p-5 flex items-start gap-4 : avatar 56×56 pill · flex-1 {h-6 w-60% ; h-3.5 w-40% mt-2} · 120×36
  region[1] chip bar      flex gap-2 overflow-hidden            : 8× Skeleton 92×32 rounded-full (clipped, not scrolling)
  region[2] health rows   GlassPanel.p-3 space-y-1              : heading 80×18 mb-2 ; 6× SkeletonRow h-11 (44pt), gap 4
  region[3] action items  GlassPanel.p-4 space-y-2              : heading 180×18 ; 2× SkeletonRow h-8  (32pt), gap 8
  region[4] resources     GlassPanel.p-4 space-y-3             : heading 120×18 ; 5× SkeletonRow h-7  (28pt), gap 12
  region[5..8] accordions 4× GlassPanel.p-5 flex items-center gap-3 : icon 20×20 · flex-1 {h-4 w-40% ; h-3 w-60% mt-1} · 60×24

  • Width-shape per block carried as fixed-pt / fraction / fill + rounded|pill (web `rounded`/`rounded-full` → pill);
    `mt-{n}` / `space-y-{n}` carried as exact web points (Tailwind 1u = 4pt); region/row gaps resolved to platform
    spacing tokens (TSSpacing) by the view → native rhythm, not ported pixels.
  • max-w-3xl (48rem = 768pt) + mx-auto reproduced as a 768pt content cap, centred.
  • A11y: the whole surface is one VoiceOver "busy" element (web role=status / aria-busy) via
    accessibilityElement(.ignore) + .updatesFrequently; the decorative shimmer blocks are accessibilityHidden; the
    busy label (web aria-label="Loading system status") resolves through the P1/S10 i18n facade (no hardcoded literal).
  • Reduce Motion: the shimmer opt-out lives in the shared TSSkeleton (prefers-reduced-motion parity). Dynamic Type:
    no fixed text; previews exercise light/dark + accessibility3.
  • P1/S11 diagnostics: emits view.opened with slug "StatusPageSkeleton" on .task (redaction-safe os_log sink).
  • Shared-component mapping: web @/components/feedback/Skeleton → TSSkeleton ; web @/components/ui GlassPanel → TSGlassPanel ;
    P1/S9 tokens TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS. No direct library imports; no charts/maps in this surface.
  • Data sources / hooks: NONE (pure presentational — the layout projection is the host-free "adapter" the tests assert).

Files shipped (7): StatusPageSkeleton.Model.swift · .Telemetry.swift · .Views.swift · .swift · .Previews.swift ·
                   .Tests.swift · .strings   (one exported View per file; barrel-free; namespaced types avoid any
                   collision with the peer LoadingSkeleton surface's Skeleton* primitives).

